From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: relay streams between the host and the machine's
 listeners

A host stream to a port a program listens on had no path in: the
kernel has IPv4 over lo only and no device. khostnetd now connects an
in-kernel TCP socket to the listener over loopback and copies bytes to
and from the host through four imports, so the program accepts an
ordinary connection and the host holds no TCP state. The listen start
and stop hooks tell the host which ports are open, the host raises
WASM_IRQ_NET when it has events, and the thread caps the client
socket's receive buffer and keeps an unsent tail per stream so a slow
side stalls the stream and not the kernel.
---
